{"id": "EUVD-2026-89431", "enisaUuid": "77493e6c-8d62-369c-a1d6-ca1802a946c1", "description": "U-Boot before 2026.10-rc4 contains an integer overflow vulnerability in sqfs_read_directory_table() function when allocating the directory table buffer. Attackers can supply a crafted SquashFS image with an attacker-controlled superblock metablks_count value that causes heap buffer under-allocation and out-of-bounds writes, corrupting heap memory and crashing the bootloader.", "datePublished": "2026-09-29T21:29:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-02T12:29:17", "baseScore": 5.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:P/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/u-boot/u-boot/commit/561ae28cb56a082cfa90c1c421c4955bc215470b", "https://github.com/u-boot/u-boot/blob/v2026.07/fs/squashfs/sqfs.c#L814", "https://github.com/u-boot/u-boot", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/u-boot-before-2026.10-rc4-integer-overflow-in-squashfs-directory-table-allocation"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-71973", "GHSA-7rqg-q392-46rw"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c8004702-4c7f-3c70-96ac-baa2d0358331", "product": {"name": "U-Boot", "vendor": {"name": "DENX Software Engineering"}}, "product_version": "0 <2026.10-rc4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5588aa98-0503-3889-8cd9-01d870acf42e", "vendor": {"name": "U-Boot"}}], "isExploited": false}